# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Secrets — the Gemini key must never reach the repo or the published site
.env

# Google service-account keys. .env only holds the PATH to one, so the key
# file itself needs its own rule or it ships with the repo. Deliberately NOT
# a blanket *.json — frontend/data/**.json is generated output that must be
# committed, or a fresh clone renders nothing.
secrets/
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
portfolio-*-*.json

# Everything generated: the formatted Excel reports, the pre-change snapshot
# store.backup() writes, and the JSON dump of the sheet taken before it was
# restructured. All of it is data, and the data lives in the Google Sheet —
# committing a copy would recreate exactly the second source of truth this
# repo no longer has.
backend/out/

# Gemini response cache. Purely a cost optimisation: the translations it
# produces are written into the IPO's YAML (the `i18n:` block) and those ARE
# committed, so a fresh clone renders every language without an API key.
backend/data/cache/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Generated at serve/deploy time from GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID. Not committed: the id
# lives in .env locally and in GitHub secrets for CI. It does become visible
# in the deployed site — the browser has to have it — but it stays out of the
# repo, and a fork points at its own sheet without editing tracked files.
frontend/js/config.js
